{
  "language_code": "en",
  "text": "Two groups of buyers did the exact same thing in Italy One of them sold for over a billion dollars the other went bankrupt I'm here in Italy to explore buying a business for myself In October 2020 three Italian luxury manufacturers combined into one group 31 months later they sold to Permira a private equity fund for over a billion dollar valuation By the time of the exit it was 26 companies over a hundred million euros in EBITDA On the other hand you have Antichi Pellettieri who did the same thing in the Italian leather goods space However at the end the company was left with almost 500 million of debt and the founders got six years each for fraudulent bankruptcy Gruppo Florence was buying B2B companies whereas Antichi was only buying B2C companies so mainly brands And every company that they bought the seller would reinvest equity or cash into the larger group and it really focused on an operations-first approach which I feel made the difference",
